raw":0.001667132,"fmt":"0.17%"},"key":"electronics-computer-distribution"},{"symbol":"^YH31130030","regMarketChangePercent":{"raw":-0.006567067,"fmt":"-0.66%"},"name":"Solar","ytdReturn":{"raw":-0.2418939,"fmt":"-24.19%"},"marketWeight":{"raw":0.001465087,"fmt":"0.15%"},"key":"solar"}],"researchReports":[{"id":"MS_0P00006TF8_AnalystReport_1791827015000","headHtml":"Analyst Report: First Solar, Inc.","provider":"Morningstar","targetPrice":191.0,"targetPriceStatus":"Decreased","investmentRating":"Neutral","reportDate":"2026-10-12T17:43:35Z","reportTitle":"First Solar designs and manufactures solar photovoltaic panels, modules, and systems primarily for use in utility-scale projects. Its modules use cadmium telluride, rather than the crystalline silicon used by most of the industry to convert sunlight into electricity. The technology does not rely on Chinese crystalline silicon supply chains. Its primary manufacturing is in the US. It has additional factories in India, Malaysia, and Vietnam. Its primary markets are the US and India. ","reportType":"Analyst Report"},{"id":"ARGUS_48507_MarketUpdate_1791825380000","headHtml":"Market Update: ODFL, OC, PLTR","provider":"Argus Research","reportDate":"2026-10-12T17:16:20Z","reportTitle":"The major stock indices are mixed at midday. The bond market is closed and equities are gearing up for earnings season. That kicks off tomorrow with the big banks, as usual, reporting on last quarter. Trading is light due to the partial U.S. holiday. Oil is up 2% at $94 per barrel and the last yield on the benchmark 10-year note was 5.24%.","reportType":"Market Update"},{"id":"ARGUS_6302_AnalystReport_1791825380000","headHtml":"Analyst Report: Palantir Technologies Inc","provider":"Argus Research","targetPrice":250.0,"targetPriceStatus":"Increased","investmentRating":"Bullish","reportDate":"2026-10-12T17:16:20Z","reportTitle":"Palantir develops and provides software that enables customers from government agencies to commercial enterprises to integrate data for decision-making and operations at scale. The company initially provided its software to the U.S. intelligence services before broadening its customer base. Palantir generates 54% of its revenue from its government segment and 46% from its commercial segment. Some 26% of revenue is generated outside the U.S. \r\n\r\nPalantir's class A shares trade publicly under the symbol PLTR. Palantir's super-voting class B and class F shares, held by insiders and founders, do not trade publicly. The company is effectively controlled by founders Alexander Karp, Stephen Cohen, and Peter Thiel, through the super-voting class F shares that represent a 49.99% voting interest. Palantir was founded in 2003 and went public at $10 per share on September 30, 2020.","reportType":"Analyst Report"},{"id":"ARGUS_48504_StockPicks_1791806181000","headHtml":"Weekly Stock List","provider":"Argus Research","reportDate":"2026-10-12T11:56:21Z","reportTitle":"Argus has published its latest Portfolio Selector, which features its popular Focus List. Each month, Director of Research Jim Kelleher, CFA, surveys the team of Argus Research industry analysts for their timeliest recommendations out of the company's fundamental universe of approximately 500 stocks. The Focus List typically includes 30 stocks: turnover is high, as Jim typically adds three or four new stocks per month. Below are the latest additions, all of which are rated BUY at Argus.","reportType":"Stock Picks"}]}}